 "_about": "Király and Tokai's set phrases: runs of signs, or one sign built of others, that their dictionary reads TOGETHER as one meaning, inside another sign's entry ('expr.' and the lists that follow it). kttranslate.phrase_slots() applies them to a line, longest first, left to right; the writers of published files (kttranslate, ktreader, ktsite) print them. Every test and gate still renders sign by sign. Key: the signs in hex, space between signs. 'slots': one word per sign in manuscript order, in this edition's words; '=' means the sign belongs to the phrase printed just before it. 'kt': their reading and the line they cite. Decided by hand, 2026-09-26, from the raw entries; phrases they mark '??' are left out, and so is one whose sense turns on context (5202c0a10850670 a10003a10060: 'nobody' in the saved-or-damned formula they cite at 019r03-04, but 'one man' at 218r and 220v; nor 6305202c1a57520, 'general' at 110v and 111v but 'on the head' at the crown of thorns, 044v and 181r), and so are phrases the sign-by-sign rendering already reads right. One-sign entries added 2026-09-28, in the hand read of this project's own readings against the dictionary: spellings their entries list under a word, or read in a worked example, that the parse of the dictionary missed, so the page cut them into pieces or printed a reading of ours instead. Each was checked at every occurrence.",

